      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's exactly what they want u to think. if it looks \"standard\" and \"formal,\" it's easier to hide in plain sight. look at the phrase \"ripple effect\" and \"monitor these changes closely\"—those feel too intentional, like they're meant to trigger something when processed by an algorithm. don't u think that even if it looks normal to a human, a machine might be picking up on a specific semantic frequency or a sequence that's been flagged? try looking deeper at the structure, not just the meaning.",
